cription":"YugabyteDB core features"},{"id":1353907004,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMzUzOTA3MDA0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/labels/priority/high","name":"priority/high","color":"ffdc5e","default":false,"description":"High Priority"}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignee":{"login":"rajukumaryb","id":49075096,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5MDc1MDk2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49075096?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajukumaryb","html_url":"https://github.com/rajukumaryb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajukumaryb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajukumaryb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajukumaryb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajukumaryb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajukumaryb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajukumaryb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajukumaryb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajukumaryb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajukumaryb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"assignees":[{"login":"rajukumaryb","id":49075096,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5MDc1MDk2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49075096?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajukumaryb","html_url":"https://github.com/rajukumaryb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajukumaryb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajukumaryb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajukumaryb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajukumaryb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajukumaryb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajukumaryb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajukumaryb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajukumaryb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajukumaryb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"milestone":null,"comments":7,"created_at":"2020-01-08T16:15:00Z","updated_at":"2020-02-07T21:50:49Z","closed_at":"2020-02-07T21:50:49Z","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"When executing concurrent write and truncate operations, we have noticed several potential race conditions, leading to SEGVs on accessing null pointers. Describing these below:\r\n\r\n1) During `Truncate`, the Tablet code will shutdown rocksdb, reset its unique_ptr and re-create it. However, the Tablet also sets up a background listener callback through `ListenFilesChanged`. Due to #3476, it is possible that the rocksdb we are closing is currently flushing/compacting a file, and, when the file is created and the callback has to be called, our rocksdb instance has already been destroyed.\r\n\r\nTo address this situation, we consider the following:\r\n- During both Truncate and Shutdown, before destroying the rocksdb instance, we can first reset the listener we have setup. This should prevent calling back code on an invalid object.\r\n- We already have a mechanism to disable flush on shutdown (for cases when we drop the table). *We can extend this to truncate as well, as we know we will not need any of these rocksdb files!*\r\n- Finally, we should standalone investigate #3476, as it's possible that there are further complications of this, or that we might end up with some in the future.\r\n\r\n2) On the leader write path, when calling `AcquireLocksAndPerformDocOperations-> StartDocWriteOperation`, we eventually require accessing the intents rocksdb for resolving conflicts. However, this path does not leverage the `pending_op_counter_`, which is what we currently use to ensure we do not operate on invalid state.\r\n\r\n3) We also noticed a race condition on followers, between processing write operations (checking rocksdb::NeedsDelay) and applying truncate operations (essentially resetting the rocksdb instance). This requires further investigation into our async model of processing and applying operations, so have filed #3477. For now, we can use the same `pending_op_counter_` mechanism to ensure that the call to `Tablet::ShouldApplyWrite` is similarly serialized, like above.","closed_by":{"login":"rajukumaryb","id":49075096,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5MDc1MDk2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49075096?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajukumaryb","html_url":"https://github.com/rajukumaryb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajukumaryb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajukumaryb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajukumaryb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajukumaryb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajukumaryb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajukumaryb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajukumaryb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajukumaryb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajukumaryb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/3288/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/3288/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}